# NOTES: learning guide and interview prep

This file is for you, not for recruiters. Read it top to bottom once, then use the interview section as flash cards. Every number here is pulled from `reports/metrics.json`, so if you quote it in an interview, it is real.

How to read the project in 30 minutes:
1. `run_pipeline.py` (the whole flow on one screen)
2. `config/contracts.yaml` (what "good data" means)
3. `sql/reconciliation/01_order_totals.sql` and `02_categorize.sql` (the core)
4. `reports/evidence/*.csv` (why the buckets exist)
5. `tests/test_validation.py` (how we prove the checks work)

