## Part 2: Decisions (every judgment call)

| Decision | Why | What I gave up |
|---|---|---|
| DuckDB, not pandas, for the heavy lifting | SQL is the skill employers test; DuckDB is fast and needs no server | pandas-only folks need to read SQL |
| Load raw as text | bad values become exceptions instead of crashes or silent NULLs | one extra staging step |
| `_row_id` as record id | natural keys are duplicated in the raw data | ids are file-position based; re-sorting the file changes them |
| Never delete, quarantine | auditability; totals stay explainable | clean views must be used deliberately |
| Reconcile on all staged rows, not the clean views | reconciliation must see both systems as they are; a duplicate payment should show as a mismatch, not vanish | DQ problems also show up as recon gaps (flagged by `has_dq_exception`) |
| Universe = union of order_ids from all 3 tables | orphans cannot hide behind a join | slightly more complex SQL |
| DECIMAL for money | exact cents | none worth mentioning |
| Tolerance R$ {{ match_tolerance_brl | num2 }} | business requirement; one cent | multi-item rounding needed its own bucket |
| Investigate before bucketing | buckets must be evidence, not guesses | took longer |
| Rounding = up to 1 cent per item | each line is rounded on its own; all small gaps were on multi-item orders | a single-item 2-cent gap is "unexplained" (strict on purpose) |
| Interest = card only, 2+ installments, overpaid | paid/sold ratio sits on fixed multipliers that rise with installments | a few orders with odd ratios are still called interest ({{ reconciliation.interest.on_shared_ratio_pct | pct }} sit on a shared ratio) |
| Discount = exactly 5% or 10% of product price, +/- 2 cents | the shortfalls land on those two values | other discount sizes fall to unexplained |
| Missing items on canceled/unavailable = medium, else high | canceled orders with payments are likely refunds; open orders with no items are a real problem | refunds are not in the data, so medium is a judgment |
| Payment sequence gap = low | {{ reconciliation.sequence_gaps.still_matched | int }} of {{ reconciliation.sequence_gaps.orders_with_sequence_gap | int }} such orders still reconcile | a real missing payment with a gap is still caught by reconciliation |
| Review id duplicate = medium, not high | the reviews are real, only the id is reused | none |
| Order category = most expensive item | one category per order for slicing | multi-category orders are simplified |
| Forecast window = longest run of complete months | edge months are near-empty and would wreck any model | fewer training months ({{ forecast.train_months | int }}) |
| Keep the baseline when it wins | honesty; a worse model is worse | less impressive-sounding |
| Plotly single HTML file | anyone can open it, no server, no Power BI license | a few MB, because the charting library is inlined |
| Docs rendered from metrics.json | no hand-typed numbers, ever | template syntax to learn |
| Large fact CSVs not committed | repo size; Parquet copies are committed | CSV users must run the pipeline |

